  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "A circular piece of paper is placed perpendicular to the projection plane, and the projection rays are perpendicular to the projection plane. What is its orthographic projection?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "A point",
    "B": "A line segment",
    "C": "A circle",
    "D": "An ellipse"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When the circular piece is perpendicular to the projection plane, the projection rays lie in the plane of the circular piece. The entire piece projects onto a line segment (whose length equals the diameter).",
